1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,680
And I love the way that the pub here the hole in the wall pub you know is built into the roman wall here.
我很喜欢这家 Hole in the Wall 酒馆的样子，它就嵌在这里的罗马城墙里。

2
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:11,720
They could make an argument that they are the oldest pub in the country could they.
他们是不是可以主张自己是全国最古老的酒馆呢？作者以问句提出这个想法。

3
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:18,590
Cuz they're built into a roman wall and the roman wall goes on for a fair old distance down here doesn't it.
因为他们建在罗马城墙里，而且城墙往这边还延伸了相当长一段，对吧？

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:32,229
We're actually going to go into the town centre and head for the castle and the roman ruins around the castle and the dutch quarter and st botolph's uh priory.
我们接下来要进入市中心，朝城堡走，看看周边的罗马遗迹、荷兰区和圣博托尔夫修道院。

5
00:00:32,239 --> 00:00:44,990
And this gateway was strengthened the walls and the gateway was strengthened to defend against the initial the early saxon raids of the 5 th century.
这座城门，还有城墙和城门，都曾加固，用来抵御五世纪早期的撒克逊人袭击；作者这样介绍。

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,720
This wall tells a story all the way through the civil war the english civil war the 1640 s when parts of it were demolished.
这面墙的故事一直延续到英国内战，也就是十七世纪四十年代，当时部分城墙被拆毁。

7
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:59,350
It's still part of the story of colchester today.
直到今天，它依然是科尔切斯特故事的一部分。

8
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:09,310
And wow I do love a water tower this is called the jumbo tower and it is a very aptly named that is the biggest water tower I have ever seen.
哇，我真喜欢水塔！这座叫 Jumbo Tower，名字很贴切；这是我见过最大的水塔。

9
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:18,510
And will just told me a great story of going up there to listen to the hare krishnas playing at the top back in the day how lovely.
Will 刚讲了个很棒的故事，以前他上去听 Hare Krishnas 在塔顶演奏，真好。

10
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:27,350
That's what an amazing water tower and I believe the mercury theatre here if I remember this correctly from what joe just told me.
真是座令人惊叹的水塔。还有这里的 Mercury Theatre，如果没记错 Joe 刚告诉我的内容……

11
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:38,510
Is based is named after a statue of mercury which was dug up in a field nearby a roman statue of mercury hence the name mercury theatre.
剧院是以附近田里挖出的墨丘利雕像命名的，那是一尊罗马雕像，所以叫 Mercury Theatre。

12
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:50,270
I've overwhelmed by the people here so lovely 100 people at the colchester arts centre and um I bumped into a few of them afterwards.
这里的人让我十分感动，大家真好。艺术中心来了大约一百人，之后我还偶遇了其中几位；overwhelmed 前的字幕语法待听辨。

13
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:59,230
Apart from cat at the venue gave me some great information must go to east hill the siege house musket ball marks in the wall there.
场地里的 Cat 给了我很好的信息：一定要去 East Hill 的 Siege House，墙上还有火枪弹痕。

14
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:03,270
Dutch quarter twinkle twinkle little star humpty dumpty we've already had.
还有荷兰区、《小星星》，以及我们已经讲过的 Humpty Dumpty。

15
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:11,200
Joe and will told me as well about same sort of lot of the same sort of stuff but also the mercury statue of mercury.
Joe 和 Will 也讲了许多类似的事，另外还介绍了那尊墨丘利雕像。

16
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:16,790
I'm already forgetting some of it now as well there's some wonderful mosaics I think in the grounds of the castle.
我现在已经忘掉一些了；我想城堡的场地里还有很漂亮的马赛克。

17
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:23,360
Some bits I won't get to like the old church that dates from the roman period I probably won't get to that today.
有些地方去不了，比如那座可追溯到罗马时期的老教堂，今天大概来不及。

18
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:30,790
But there's obviously lots to come back to colchester for but we're going to try and do as much of the kind of heritage y stuff as we can.
不过科尔切斯特显然还有很多值得再来的理由；我们会尽量多看一些历史文化方面的地方。

19
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:35,560
And paul and his wife who dispensed a lot of really invaluable information as well.
Paul 和他的妻子也给了我许多特别宝贵的信息。

20
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:39,110
So I think between all of them I'm going to try and hold it in my head.
综合他们说的这些，我要尽量把信息都记在脑子里。

21
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:42,400
Maybe I'll just jot it down quickly so I don't forget too much of it.
也许还是赶快记下来，这样就不至于忘掉太多。

22
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:50,470
This is going to be amazing I I I've only been here I became acquainted to doing the talk outside the venue been outside the venue for about 20 minutes.
这次一定很精彩。我才来不久，刚做完讲座、在场地外面，大约待了二十分钟；中间的 acquainted 连接句字幕不明。

23
00:02:50,480 --> 00:03:03,070
Bowled over already so we go down church street here towards the high street.
已经被深深打动了。我们沿 Church Street 往商业大街走。

24
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:09,160
And the high street sits on the top of north hill here and that is one hell of a climb up there.
商业大街位于 North Hill 顶上；往上爬可真够费劲的。

25
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:18,320
You can see why people built a castle here cymbeline in 50 bc an iron age stronghold.
这就能理解为什么人们在此建城堡了。作者接着提到公元前50年的辛白林，这里是铁器时代的要塞。

26
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:28,600
It would have been impregnable to everyone apart from the emperor claudius who brought his elephants in order to conquer britain.
它大概对谁都难以攻破，除了克劳狄乌斯皇帝；作者说他为征服不列颠带来了大象。

27
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:34,160
And these elephant wayfinders around colchester are a reminder of that.
科尔切斯特各处这些大象形状的导向标识，就是在提醒人们这段故事。

28
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:42,470
That's a beautiful old essex and suffolk fire office building here at the edge of the high street.
这里这幢老 Essex and Suffolk Fire Office 楼真漂亮，就在商业大街边上。

29
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:49,270
And that pub over there is the original name of colchester the brythonic name.
那边那家酒馆用的是科尔切斯特原来的名字，也就是布立吞语名称；这是作者的解释。

30
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:53,900
And it is a really fine high street isn't it really fine high street.
这确实是一条很漂亮的商业大街，不是吗？真漂亮。
